        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0039" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg31"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.01/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-21T21:00:00+07:00">June 21, 1940—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 21—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram dated June 20, 11 a.m.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d45-f1"/>
                    The situation here appears to have improved considerably within the last 24
                    hours but preparations for defense are being methodically expedited.</p>
                <p>I was informed by the Governor General late this afternoon that he intended to
                    defend Indochina at all costs. While he expressed hope that the United States
                    would exert influence to maintain the <hi rendition="#italic">status guo</hi> in
                    the Far East, he emphasized the hope that several hundred airplanes could be
                    made available in the near future to be followed by other needed munitions of
                    war. He suggested that these supplies might be taken from those ordered
                    previously for France. He expressed regret that circumstances have forced the
                    closing of this [area?] for American goods.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department naval radio Cavite for repetition to the Consulate [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Embassy?</hi>] Chungking [and] confirmation copies Hong
                    Kong.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
